  "construction": "Prescribed source definitions and public getter prompts and mouse rays supply inputs. Analytic lines/arcs and exact dyadic Bernstein sphere crossings supply setbacks. NURBS interval edits use portable/usd-brep producers. Native output coefficients and 33 original point/tangent samples per curve are expectations.",
  "execution": "Licensed Rhino ran on private Xvfb displays; egui viewport tests were windowless. Two unsuccessful cancellation drivers published zero observations and were stopped only after owned process verification. The pilot physical Escape driver predates external_keys export; its frozen driver, sent Escape and public Cancel are retained. Discovery and holdouts additionally record external key delivery.",
  "limits": [
    "Oversized distance 9 on a length-4 line is a captured native success whose retained line ends at x=13 while its bevel begins at x=-5. Viboceros rejects this case atomically; it is excluded from geometry parity.",
    "Same-parent and closed-source Chamfer are unsupported. This finite corpus does not qualify arbitrary folded curves, all intersection branches, pixel equality or comparative performance. Bare other-curve extension toggling follows the two-value UI convention but has no dedicated native trajectory in this corpus.",
    "The discovery measurement recipe supplies a redundant second anchor. Native accepts a zero second distance and ignores the subsequent coordinate at source selection; that trajectory is retained, and the holdout supplies the intended shared-anchor measurement."
  ],
